# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF line endings, on Windows too, so a checkout there never rewrites
# files (and their tests, which compare exact bytes, still pass). Git leaves binary files alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Test videos are bytes, never text, whatever git guesses.
*.ivf binary
# Two stacks of PRs each add rows to the plan's tables, and the rows never depend on each other: a merge keeps both
# sides' lines rather than stopping at a conflict (Kevin, Nov 20). A merge that comes out with a wrong or doubled row
# means this line goes again.
docs/PLAN.md merge=union
